      "id": 1,
      "text": "Front Royal’s name may come from a giant oak tree called the “Royal Tree of England” that once stood where Chester and Main Streets meet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Front_Royal%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During the Civil War, Front Royal became a strategic rail hub when the line extended to Strasburg, setting the stage for the 1862 Battle of Front Royal.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Front_Royal%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Front Royal sits where the North and South Forks of the Shenandoah River merge, a spot that shaped its early trade routes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Front_Royal%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Front Royal hosts Randolph‑Macon Academy, a private school founded in 1892 that still draws students from across the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Front_Royal%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Bing Crosby helped fund Front Royal’s original stadium by premiering his film Riding High there on April 1, 1950.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
